{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>ומעת</b> — I have explained it. And after it is said: אשרי המחכה ויגיע. The sense is that this number is like half a week, and behold, close to three and a half years the Second Temple stood without an offering [עולה] and afterward was destroyed, and Israel went into exile. And close to this number Israel will stand in a great trouble such as never was, with the little horn, and it is the kingdom of Ishmael, for most of the exile is in their land. And this is יתיהבון בידיה (\"they will be given into his hand\") עד עדן עידנין ופלג עדן. And there is no mark for years in Aramaic as there is in the sacred tongue — שנתים is dual; and the proof falls upon one of the two, and the plural form דרכים — the minimum is three. Therefore it is written עדן, one year, like למועדה מימים ימימה. And behold ועדנין — three and a half years. Therefore we have need, and this is למועד מועדים וחצי, for למועד serves as in למועד חדש האביב, and behold מועדים — three; and because half a year is approximate, there was need to specify the number of days, and this is אשרי המחכה ויגיע. And the sense is that he will endure the great trouble, for there it is written להשניא זמנין. And the religion of the companion of Daniel [n] joins these numbers that are not at one time, because close to the number of days that Jerusalem stood in trouble before the exile is like their number, so will be the days that Israel will stand in great trouble before the coming of the redeemer. And behold, it is confirmed according to this interpretation, that when the king of the North goes forth and takes Egypt after three and a half, the redeemer will come to Israel — only we do not know until now when this aforementioned king went forth to the land of Egypt."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Reading ודת חבר דניאל as 'and the religion of the companion of Daniel'; the phrase is elliptic and possibly corrupt, but rendered hyper-literally without emendation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:36.238714627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}